<title>USA: Paxar to acquire Taiwanese company.</title>
<headline>Paxar to acquire Taiwanese company.</headline>
<dateline>WHITE PLAINS, N.Y. 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paxar Corp said Tuesday it has signed a letter of intent to acquire the Golden-State Group of companies based in Taipei, Taiwan for $23 million in cash and stock.</p>
<p>The transaction is expected to close in 90 days.</p>
<p>Golden-State produces label fabrics for the apparel and textile industries. Its founders and principal owners, Grace Ro and C.T. Ro, will continue to manage the business.</p>
<p>Paxar manufactures identification products and systems for the apparel and textile industries.</p>
</text>
